<DocsExample TExample="HeatMapBasicExample" Title="Basic heat map" Description="A heat map shades each cell by its weight. Use it to find busy and quiet periods across two dimensions, such as weekday and hour." />
<DocsExample TExample="HeatMapRowLabelsExample" Title="Row labels" Description="The Y axis puts one tick on each row. Give NTYAxisOptions a LabelFormatter to name the rows, here turning a month number into a month and year. The tooltip names the hovered row the same way." />
<DocsExample TExample="HeatMapColorsExample" Title="Colors and cell padding" Description="MinColor and MaxColor set the color scale, and CellPadding sets the gap between cells in dp. Match the colors to what the data means, and use a larger gap to separate cells." />
